Not vendored: recording.ts (the rrweb DOM tape), tests, gen.ts, repl.ts, the protocol JSON.

Local patches, copied from flow-pilot's vendor/bhjs and being upstreamed to
github.com/monotykamary/browser-harness-js in parallel. Drop each one here
once the upstream commit that carries it is vendored:
- interaction.ts: a transparent native checkbox, radio, file input or select
  laid over its own drawn proxy is operable where the hit test lands on it.
- interaction.ts: FLOW_PILOT_ALLOW_SENSITIVE=1 keeps credential and
  personal-data fields operable (read when used, not at import). The Midscene
  device sets it only around its own guarded calls (allowSensitiveFields).
- page.ts: cross-origin frames no longer count toward the frame limit (64).
- page.ts: role locators resolve on large pages (maxChars 1,000,000).
- page.ts: frames the guard cannot read (cross-origin, not committed) do not
  make a role locator ambiguous.
- page.ts: guarded refusals say why (disabled, hidden by ..., pointer-only,
  off-screen, covered by ..., not a control).

No other changes. Keep this directory out of the formatter and linter
(biome.json files.ignore) so it stays byte-comparable with upstream.
